        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Bethany, this is a beautiful mission your sister is taking on. A **GoFundMe that feels heartfelt, urgent, and credible** tends to perform best. You want people to feel the **emotional pull of the cats**, but also see **a clear plan** for what the money will do.\n\n### Recommended Goal Amount\nFor GoFundMe, it is usually better to start with a **specific but achievable number**.\n\n**My recommendation:**  \n**$5,000 starting goal**\n\nReasons:\n- $3,000 can look small for a sanctuary build.\n- $10K+ can feel overwhelming for first-time donors.\n- $5K feels **serious but reachable** and you can always raise the goal later if momentum builds.\n\nIf she already has a network that will donate quickly, you could start at **$7,500**.\n\n---\n\n# GoFundMe Draft\n\n**Title Ideas**\n- Help Us Build a Safe Haven for Community Cats on Hawaii\u2019s Big Island  \n- Urgent: Help Save Community Cats from Starvation on the Big Island  \n- Creating a Cat Sanctuary for Hawaii\u2019s Abandoned Community Cats  \n\n---\n\n## Help Us Build a Safe Haven for Community Cats on Hawaii\u2019s Big Island\n\nMy husband and I are following our hearts and beginning the journey of building a **cat rescue sanctuary on the Big Island of Hawaii**.\n\nEvery day here, community cats are facing **death from starvation, abuse, and neglect**.\n\nMany of these cats were once pets that were **illegally dumped by residents**, yet the problem continues to spiral out of control. The cats left behind are forced to fend for themselves with no safe place to go.\n\nRecently, **Bill 51 was enacted by the county**, which states that animals cannot be fed on county property. Those who attempt to feed them risk **fines and even jail time**.\n\nThis has created a heartbreaking situation where the very people trying to help these animals are now being penalized for showing compassion.\n\nMeanwhile, **vigilantes have begun taking matters into their own hands**, targeting community cats and those who care for them. Myself and the **thousands of volunteers who help community cats** now live with fear for our safety while simply trying to protect these innocent animals.\n\nThese cats did not choose this life.  \nThey were abandoned.\n\nAnd they deserve better.\n\nThat is why we are building a **community cat sanctuary** where feral and abandoned cats can finally have:\n\n\u2022 Safety  \n\u2022 Food and clean water  \n\u2022 Medical care  \n\u2022 Warm beds and blankets  \n\u2022 A place to live without fear  \n\u2022 The chance to be adopted into loving homes  \n\nCreating this sanctuary requires a tremendous amount of resources. The costs of **medical care, building materials, food, traps, microchip scanners, bedding, blankets, and rescue supplies** add up quickly.\n\nWe are asking for your help to raise **$5,000** to help us complete the sanctuary as quickly as possible so we can begin bringing these cats to safety.\n\nEvery dollar raised will go directly toward:\n\n- Building safe cat enclosures and shelter space  \n- Veterinary care and vaccinations  \n- Food and daily care supplies  \n- Humane traps and rescue equipment  \n- Microchip scanners and medical supplies  \n- Beds, blankets, and enrichment items  \n\nThese cats deserve a chance to live without fear.\n\nWith your support, we can create a place where abandoned and feral cats are **loved, protected, and given a real chance at life.**\n\nEven the smallest donation helps save a life.\n\nIf you cannot donate, please consider **sharing our story** so more people can help these innocent animals.\n\nFrom the bottom of our hearts, thank you for helping us build a safer future for Hawaii\u2019s community cats.\n\n\u2764\ufe0f\n\n---\n\nIf you'd like, I can also help you with:\n\n\u2022 **A shorter version that converts better on GoFundMe**  \n\u2022 **Photos to include that increase donations**  \n\u2022 **A viral Facebook post that will drive traffic to the GoFundMe**  \n\u2022 **A headline that raises 2\u20133x more donations**\n\nThose things can make a **huge difference in how much she raises.**"
